- [exhales shakily]
- Two, three, four.

233
00:11:02,417 --> 00:11:03,251
You got this.

234
00:11:04,209 --> 00:11:05,084
[mouths]

235
00:11:06,959 --> 00:11:08,667
[Mallory] That's it.

236
00:11:08,751 --> 00:11:11,584
- [TJ] Hey. Was it good? Yeah?
- [chuckles] It was good.

237
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:13,584
[seat hinges grinding loudly]

238
00:11:15,876 --> 00:11:17,126
Sorry.

239
00:11:34,417 --> 00:11:38,917
<i>♪ What if when he sees me</i>
<i>I like him and he knows it? ♪</i>

240
00:11:39,001 --> 00:11:45,292
<i>♪ What if he opens up a door</i>
<i>And I can't close it? ♪</i>

241
00:11:45,376 --> 00:11:46,959
[sniffles]

242
00:11:47,042 --> 00:11:50,709
<i>♪ What happens then? ♪</i>

243
00:11:50,792 --> 00:11:54,042
<i>♪ If when he holds me ♪</i>

244
00:11:54,126 --> 00:11:56,417
<i>♪ My heart is set in motion ♪</i>

245
00:11:56,501 --> 00:11:58,084
<i>♪ I'm not prepared for that ♪</i>

246
00:11:58,167 --> 00:12:02,792
<i>♪I'm scared of breaking open ♪</i>

247
00:12:04,292 --> 00:12:09,376
<i>♪ But still I can't help from hoping ♪</i>

248
00:12:12,376 --> 00:12:18,667
<i>♪ To find someone to talk to ♪</i>

249
00:12:19,626 --> 00:12:25,459
<i>♪ Who likes the way I am ♪</i>

250
00:12:26,334 --> 00:12:31,126
<i>♪ Someone who, when he sees me ♪</i>

251
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:32,917
[breathing shakily]

252
00:12:33,001 --> 00:12:39,334
<i>♪ Wants to again ♪</i>

253
00:12:42,959 --> 00:12:44,126
[applause]

254
00:12:53,876 --> 00:12:54,834
Hi!

255
00:12:54,917 --> 00:12:57,292
- [Ted] How'd the audition go?
- [brother] I want him not to run!

256
00:12:57,376 --> 00:12:59,084
- [Sophie] It was fine.
- My turn! Me first!

257
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:00,876
- [Sophie] Get off. Stop.
- Boys, boys, boys.

258
00:13:00,959 --> 00:13:03,667
- [Elizabeth] Boys, be gentle.
- [Ted] Hey. I got ya. I got ya.

259
00:13:03,751 --> 00:13:06,584
There must be more to the story
than "fine," right?

260
00:13:07,292 --> 00:13:08,209
I don't know.

261
00:13:08,709 --> 00:13:11,376
[Ted] Hey, guys, uh… why don't we
go to the living room for a minute?

262
00:13:11,459 --> 00:13:13,501
Mom and I need
to talk to you about something.

263
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,001
Come on, Soph.

264
00:13:20,792 --> 00:13:23,501
- ["A Good Thing" by Claud playing]
- [phone ringing]

265
00:13:24,959 --> 00:13:26,917
<i>♪ Don't try and fix it if-- ♪</i>

266
00:13:27,001 --> 00:13:28,917
- [turns music off]
- [phone chimes]

267
00:13:29,792 --> 00:13:31,209
It came back.

268
00:13:32,501 --> 00:13:33,334
[Carolyn] <i>No.</i>

269
00:13:33,834 --> 00:13:35,876
Yeah. They said she's gonna fight it.

270
00:13:36,876 --> 00:13:38,792
To figure out a treatment plan, but…

271
00:13:38,876 --> 00:13:42,251
Right. And they figured it out
last time, so…

272
00:13:43,709 --> 00:13:45,667
I don't want anyone to know.

273
00:13:45,751 --> 00:13:47,292
<i>I totally get that.</i>

274
00:13:48,626 --> 00:13:50,417
I'm here for you. Okay?

275
00:13:51,292 --> 00:13:52,584
Always.

276
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:57,292
They didn't even tell me
they were going in today.

277
00:13:57,792 --> 00:13:59,542
She didn't even seem like she…

278
00:14:02,001 --> 00:14:03,251
I'm gonna go.

279
00:14:03,792 --> 00:14:05,292
- Soph…
- [disconnection tone beeps]

280
00:14:10,292 --> 00:14:11,709
[sobbing]

281
00:14:11,792 --> 00:14:13,792
[poignant music playing]

282
00:14:44,959 --> 00:14:46,126
[Trista] <i>The cast list is out!</i>

283
00:14:46,792 --> 00:14:50,626
Attention all thespians,
the cast list is out!

284
00:14:51,209 --> 00:14:52,501
- Sorry!
- [girl 1] Trista!

285
00:14:53,042 --> 00:14:54,251
Are you ready?

286
00:14:54,917 --> 00:14:58,209
- Mmm… I don't know.
- [lockers open and slam]

287
00:14:58,292 --> 00:15:01,501
- You don't have to do it, you know.
- Uh, what?

288
00:15:01,584 --> 00:15:03,751
I'm not trying to be rude.
It's just, you're a sophomore.

289
00:15:03,834 --> 00:15:07,042
I mean… have you ever even done
a summer intensive?

290
00:15:07,126 --> 00:15:09,334
Wait, I'm so confused. Did I get Dawn?

291
00:15:09,417 --> 00:15:10,667
I'm gonna get in there.

292
00:15:12,334 --> 00:15:13,376
I got Dawn.

293
00:15:14,334 --> 00:15:15,417
Mal… Mal, let's just…

294
00:15:16,126 --> 00:15:18,376
[Carolyn] Um… Sophie?

295
00:15:19,209 --> 00:15:20,626
[exciting music playing]

296
00:15:20,709 --> 00:15:21,876
[girl 2] Here she is.

297
00:15:29,917 --> 00:15:31,126
[Ted] Guys, there you go.

298
00:15:31,209 --> 00:15:32,501
[entry bell jangles]

299
00:15:32,584 --> 00:15:33,667
I got the lead.

300
00:15:34,334 --> 00:15:35,709
Oh, hey. What's up?

301
00:15:36,292 --> 00:15:37,626
I got the lead.

302
00:15:39,167 --> 00:15:40,584
Annie? You got Annie?

303
00:15:40,667 --> 00:15:42,042
- [Ted] What do you mean, Annie?
- Yeah.

304
00:15:42,126 --> 00:15:44,501
- No, she got the… the lead. Jenna.
- You got the <i>lead </i>lead?

305
00:15:44,584 --> 00:15:45,709
The… the lead, the Annie?

306
00:15:45,792 --> 00:15:47,292
- Yes.
- Whoa!

307
00:15:47,376 --> 00:15:49,459
- [Ted] Congratulations.
- [Lenny] Mazel tov, Sophie.

308
00:15:49,542 --> 00:15:52,292
- [Elizabeth] Ooh!
- [Ted] My baby got the lead in the play!

309
00:15:52,376 --> 00:15:55,251
- Oh, we have to go eat and celebrate.
- [Ted] Yeah, yeah. We'll go out.

310
00:15:55,334 --> 00:15:59,001
<i>♪ The sun'll come out tomorrow ♪</i>

311
00:15:59,084 --> 00:16:02,959
<i>- ♪ Bet your bottom dollar that tomorrow ♪</i>
- [Ted joins in] <i>♪Tomorrow ♪</i>

312
00:16:03,042 --> 00:16:05,626
<i>♪ There'll be sun ♪</i>

313
00:16:05,709 --> 00:16:08,209
<i>♪ Tomorrow, tomorr-- ♪</i>

314
00:16:08,292 --> 00:16:10,209
Musicals are stupid.

315
00:16:10,292 --> 00:16:11,876
Oh, come on, buddy. Don't say stupid.

316
00:16:11,959 --> 00:16:13,792
Why do they sing? Just be talking.

317
00:16:13,876 --> 00:16:17,584
Because music can make you feel things
that are bigger than just talking, Caleb.

318
00:16:17,667 --> 00:16:22,501
It shows people going through stuff,
like when things are hard or fun.

319
00:16:22,584 --> 00:16:24,501
You can see how
other people go through that too.

320
00:16:24,584 --> 00:16:26,042
What's the stuff in your one?

321
00:16:26,126 --> 00:16:29,459
Well, I play Jenna,
who is pregnant and bakes pies.

322
00:16:29,542 --> 00:16:31,209
And her husband…

323
00:16:31,292 --> 00:16:34,667
isn't nice like Dad, and then
she falls in love with her gynecologist.

324
00:16:34,751 --> 00:16:36,334
- Her what?
- [Ted] Wait, hold on.

325
00:16:36,417 --> 00:16:38,084
Wasn't last year, like, fairy tales?

326
00:16:38,667 --> 00:16:40,667
- It was Sondheim.
- [woman] Elizabeth.

327
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:42,209
Hi, Shelly.

328
00:16:42,917 --> 00:16:44,292
I just heard.

329
00:16:44,376 --> 00:16:45,501
I'm so sorry.

330
00:16:46,126 --> 00:16:47,167
Um…

331
00:16:47,251 --> 00:16:51,542
We are actually celebrating Sophie
tonight. She got the lead in her play.

332
00:16:51,626 --> 00:16:54,459
And you brought her to Lee's.
You're such a good mom.

333
00:16:54,542 --> 00:16:56,376
You're gonna beat it just like last time.

334
00:16:56,459 --> 00:17:00,626
I said to June Nizio,
"I can't believe out of everyone…"

335
00:17:00,709 --> 00:17:02,376
[Sophie] <i>Mom, maybe</i>
<i>I shouldn't do the show.</i>

336
00:17:02,459 --> 00:17:04,417
- [Elizabeth] Of course you should.
- [boys barking]

337
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:07,251
[Elizabeth] I love watching you perform.

338
00:17:07,334 --> 00:17:10,667
I will never forget your first solo.

339
00:17:10,751 --> 00:17:12,584
- The second-grade concert.
- [Ted] The back seat.

340
00:17:12,667 --> 00:17:18,126
<i>- ♪ You just gotta ignite the light ♪</i>
- Oh, please don't do this.

341
00:17:18,209 --> 00:17:22,167
<i>- ♪ And let it shine ♪</i>
- [Sophie laughs]

342
00:17:22,251 --> 00:17:25,042
<i>- ♪ Just own the night ♪</i>
- [Sophie] Mom!

343
00:17:25,126 --> 00:17:28,126
- Stop!
<i>- ♪ Like the 4th of July ♪</i>

344
00:17:28,209 --> 00:17:29,334
Okay, enough.

345
00:17:29,417 --> 00:17:32,917
<i>♪ 'Cause baby, you're a fire… ♪ </i>[chuckles]

346
00:17:33,001 --> 00:17:35,626
- You were so good, though.
- Thank you.

347
00:17:35,709 --> 00:17:38,001
- I cried so much. Oh.
- [gentle music playing]

348
00:17:38,501 --> 00:17:39,667
Get ready to weep.

349
00:17:39,751 --> 00:17:42,334
Okay, I'm gonna put it in the calendar.

350
00:17:43,084 --> 00:17:45,417
What are the exact dates?

351
00:17:45,501 --> 00:17:48,376
- Uh, May 15th and 16th.
- Okay.

352
00:17:48,917 --> 00:17:49,959
15th… Oh.

353
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:54,084
It's just a couple of weeks
before the beach rental.

354
00:17:54,167 --> 00:17:55,709
This is gonna be great.

355
00:17:56,417 --> 00:17:57,834
We're still going?

356
00:17:59,542 --> 00:18:01,084
To the Crane House?

357
00:18:02,084 --> 00:18:04,626
Honey, yeah.
Of course we're going to the beach.

358
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:06,709
- We always go to the beach.
- [car starts]

359
00:18:06,792 --> 00:18:09,084
[boys barking and growling]

360
00:18:10,959 --> 00:18:13,251
[Ted] Please get in.
They've been doing this the whole time.

361
00:18:13,334 --> 00:18:15,292
- [Elizabeth] I'm sorry.
- What are you doing out here?

362
00:18:15,376 --> 00:18:16,626
- [Elizabeth] Talking.
- [Sophie] Yeah.

363
00:18:16,709 --> 00:18:18,709
- [pop music playing]
- [girl] Yeah, sounds nice.

364
00:18:19,542 --> 00:18:21,167
[laughter]

365
00:18:29,167 --> 00:18:30,542
[boy] Nice highlighting.

366
00:18:30,626 --> 00:18:32,501
[Sophie] Oh, um… it's just normal.

367
00:18:32,584 --> 00:18:34,959
- Here. You can have it.
- But you're not done.

368
00:18:35,042 --> 00:18:39,917
Uh… No, I like to take highlighter breaks
so I don't get carpal tunnel syndrome.

369
00:18:40,001 --> 00:18:43,084
Have you heard of carpal tunnel?
It… it affects your ligaments.

370
00:18:43,167 --> 00:18:44,251
Sophie, right?

371
00:18:44,334 --> 00:18:46,917
Uh, that is indeed my name.

372
00:18:47,001 --> 00:18:49,084
I'm Jack. I'm playing Dr. Pomatter.

373
00:18:49,167 --> 00:18:52,042
Yeah. We're gonna do
a lot of fun stuff together

374
00:18:52,542 --> 00:18:53,626
onstage.

375
00:18:59,292 --> 00:19:00,459
Oh.

376
00:19:00,542 --> 00:19:01,626
[door opens]

377
00:19:01,709 --> 00:19:03,042
[Ms. Parker] Hello, thespians!

378
00:19:03,626 --> 00:19:04,959
Let's rehearse.

379
00:19:08,876 --> 00:19:10,792
Can you feel my hand and how sweaty it is?

380
00:19:10,876 --> 00:19:12,126
Yeah. Hmm.

381
00:19:12,209 --> 00:19:15,667
It's slimy, it's clammy, it's oddly hot.

382
00:19:15,751 --> 00:19:18,834
- All the things you don't want it to be.
- Aw, thank you.

383
00:19:18,917 --> 00:19:20,626
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

384
00:19:20,709 --> 00:19:23,417
[group repeating] One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

385
00:19:23,501 --> 00:19:25,584
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven, eight.

386
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:28,417
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven!

387
00:19:28,501 --> 00:19:31,167
One, two, three, four.
One, two, three, four.

388
00:19:31,251 --> 00:19:33,209
One, two, three. One, two, three.

389
00:19:33,292 --> 00:19:34,834
One, two. One, two. One, two, one.

390
00:19:34,917 --> 00:19:36,792
One! One! One! One! One!

391
00:19:36,876 --> 00:19:40,959
[all shout, one at a time] Wah! Wah! Wah!
Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah! Wah!

392
00:19:41,042 --> 00:19:42,376
[clapping]

393
00:19:42,459 --> 00:19:44,501
[chanting rhythmically]

394
00:19:44,584 --> 00:19:45,917
- [girl 1] Cherry!
- [Sophie] Oi!

395
00:19:46,001 --> 00:19:47,584
- [girl 1] Bufala!
- [Sophie] Cherry!

396
00:19:47,667 --> 00:19:48,876
- [girl 1] Orange.
- [Mallory] Oi!

397
00:19:48,959 --> 00:19:50,334
- [girl 1] Bufala.
- [Mallory] Apple.

398
00:19:50,417 --> 00:19:51,584
- [girl 1] Apple.
- [boy 1] Oi!

399
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:53,042
- [girl 1] Bufala.
- [Sophie] Pineapple.

400
00:19:53,126 --> 00:19:54,167
- [girl 1] Pineapple.
- [Mr. Stewart] Oi!

401
00:19:54,251 --> 00:19:55,084
[girl 1] Bufala.

402
00:19:55,167 --> 00:19:59,459
- Passion fruit! Passion fruit!
- [all] Oi, oi, oi! Oh!

403
00:20:01,209 --> 00:20:02,792
Hi, I'm Dr. Pomatter.

404
00:20:02,876 --> 00:20:06,251
I just moved here from Connecticut,
and I'm a gynecologist.

405
00:20:07,126 --> 00:20:10,251
[Southern accent] Hi, my name's Jebba…
I… I mean, Jenna.

406
00:20:10,334 --> 00:20:14,001
- And, um, my baby's got a belly in it.
- [group giggling and whispering]

407
00:20:14,084 --> 00:20:15,376
[Southern accent] My name's Dawn,

408
00:20:15,459 --> 00:20:17,792
and my baby certainly
does not have a belly in it!

409
00:20:17,876 --> 00:20:18,751
[laughter]

410
00:20:18,834 --> 00:20:21,126
And my heart belongs
to the History Channel.

411
00:20:21,209 --> 00:20:22,084
- Mm-hmm.
- Oh!

412
00:20:22,167 --> 00:20:27,292
[exaggeratedly] I'm old Joe, the diner
owner, and my body's deterioratin'.

413
00:20:27,376 --> 00:20:28,376
[laughter]

414
00:20:28,459 --> 00:20:32,001
I play ensemble-slash-pie shop
customer number three,

415
00:20:32,084 --> 00:20:35,209
and you don't want to go in my basement.

416
00:20:35,292 --> 00:20:36,626
- [giggles]
- Huh?

417
00:20:39,417 --> 00:20:40,709
[keys jangle]

418
00:20:40,792 --> 00:20:43,334
Who's ready for a driving lesson?

419
00:20:44,251 --> 00:20:46,167
Oh, no! What's wrong?

420
00:20:50,459 --> 00:20:52,792
- Okay. No driving lesson?
- [door slams]

421
00:20:53,501 --> 00:20:55,501
[car door alarm pinging]

422
00:20:57,959 --> 00:20:58,876
What happened?

423
00:20:58,959 --> 00:21:02,417
Everyone's accent sounds so good,
and I sound…

424
00:21:02,501 --> 00:21:04,542
ugh, like a cartoon rooster.

425
00:21:05,542 --> 00:21:07,417
Mom, it's not funny.

426
00:21:08,042 --> 00:21:08,876
Sorry.

427
00:21:10,001 --> 00:21:12,042
Maybe Ms. Parker made a mistake.

428
00:21:15,209 --> 00:21:16,251
You know what?

429
00:21:17,792 --> 00:21:19,292
I think I have an idea.

430
00:21:19,376 --> 00:21:21,417
[starts engine]

431
00:21:22,959 --> 00:21:24,959
- Mom, where are we even going?
- Hmm… Mmm!

432
00:21:25,584 --> 00:21:26,542
[clears throat]

433
00:21:29,876 --> 00:21:32,959
[Southern accent] Uh, excuse me, Angel.

434
00:21:33,042 --> 00:21:36,709
Ahem. My daughter and I
are visitin' from Georgia,

435
00:21:36,792 --> 00:21:40,542
and we're lookin' to buy
some bathin' suits.

436
00:21:41,251 --> 00:21:44,376
Why don't you tell the nice lady
what kind of suit you want?

437
00:21:44,459 --> 00:21:46,167
No, it's… it's fine.

438
00:21:46,834 --> 00:21:50,834
Go ahead.
Tell her what kind of suit you fancy.

439
00:21:50,917 --> 00:21:52,626
Um…

440
00:21:52,709 --> 00:21:55,167
[Southern accent] Somethin', uh… sparkly.

441
00:21:55,251 --> 00:21:56,501
Sparkly.

442
00:21:57,584 --> 00:21:58,626
And what else?

443
00:21:59,959 --> 00:22:01,251
With ruffles.

444
00:22:01,334 --> 00:22:02,709
- Ruffles.
- Mm-hmm.

445
00:22:03,376 --> 00:22:04,667
We don't really have that.

446
00:22:04,751 --> 00:22:06,042
Well, y'all should.

447
00:22:06,126 --> 00:22:10,709
My daughter is Miss Savannah,
and y'all just lost her business.

448
00:22:14,376 --> 00:22:16,626
- Bless your heart.
- [giggles]

449
00:22:16,709 --> 00:22:18,959
["Tiny Moves" by Bleachers playing]

450
00:22:21,001 --> 00:22:23,001
- [Elizabeth] Ooh.
- [Sophie] Oh.

451
00:22:23,542 --> 00:22:27,251
This chair is just much too firm
for my lil' bottom.

452
00:22:27,334 --> 00:22:30,584
And this one's just too tiny
for my big 'un.

453
00:22:30,667 --> 00:22:33,667
- [normally] Honey, you have the best butt.
- Mom, don't do that.

454
00:22:36,959 --> 00:22:37,876
[Southern accent] Oh!

455
00:22:39,126 --> 00:22:40,542
It spins!

456
00:22:40,626 --> 00:22:42,084
Fancy!

457
00:22:42,167 --> 00:22:43,542
- [chairs rumbling]
- [both giggling]

458
00:22:43,626 --> 00:22:44,959
<i>♪ Whoa, oh, oh! ♪</i>

459
00:22:45,792 --> 00:22:47,792
<i>♪ Watchin' it all come down ♪</i>

460
00:22:48,834 --> 00:22:51,126
<i>♪ Watch it go round and round… ♪</i>

461
00:22:51,209 --> 00:22:55,126
[Southern accent] I'll have ten
of your finest buttermilk biscuits

462
00:22:55,209 --> 00:22:56,917
and a gallon of sweet tea.

463
00:22:59,167 --> 00:23:00,584
This is a pizza place.

464
00:23:00,667 --> 00:23:03,084
<i>♪ On the edge again, on the edge again… ♪</i>

465
00:23:03,167 --> 00:23:05,126
- [Elizabeth laughing] Oh!
- [Sophie] Hey!

466
00:23:05,209 --> 00:23:07,126
[Elizabeth] <i>"Now remember what I said."</i>

467
00:23:07,209 --> 00:23:10,126
"Don't you go lovin' that baby
more than me."

468
00:23:10,667 --> 00:23:15,209
"I don't love you anymore, Earl.
I haven't in a very long time."

469
00:23:18,667 --> 00:23:19,834
What?

470
00:23:21,251 --> 00:23:23,876
Ms. Parker didn't make a mistake.

471
00:23:30,334 --> 00:23:31,626
[sighs]

472
00:23:31,709 --> 00:23:34,084
Ahem. "That's not funny, Jenna."

473
00:23:34,167 --> 00:23:35,959
[Sophie] <i>♪ She is messy ♪</i>

474
00:23:36,626 --> 00:23:39,167
<i>- ♪ But she's kind ♪</i>
- [mouthing]

475
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:44,709
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

476
00:23:44,792 --> 00:23:46,876
- Okay, uh, let's pause.
- [piano stops]

477
00:23:47,584 --> 00:23:48,917
- [sighs]
- [Ms. Parker] Um…

478
00:23:49,917 --> 00:23:51,376
What are you feeling right now?

479
00:23:51,459 --> 00:23:54,501
Uh, like I need a lot more practice.

480
00:23:54,584 --> 00:23:57,001
Well, that's Sophie. You're Jenna.

481
00:23:58,542 --> 00:23:59,626
Jenna,

482
00:24:00,376 --> 00:24:04,459
everything in her life
has built to this moment right now.

483
00:24:04,542 --> 00:24:06,834
Yeah, I know. I just…
I really want to get the notes right.

484
00:24:07,417 --> 00:24:09,417
Forget about the notes, all right?

485
00:24:11,501 --> 00:24:14,126
I want you to mess up.

486
00:24:14,917 --> 00:24:16,626
That's how you get to the good stuff.

487
00:24:17,126 --> 00:24:19,126
There's so much going on
in your life right now.

488
00:24:19,209 --> 00:24:22,626
- What are you talking about?
- You're gonna have a baby, Jenna.

489
00:24:24,126 --> 00:24:25,251
Right.

490
00:24:26,334 --> 00:24:28,751
[Ms. Parker] Right. So put it in the song.

491
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:29,959
- Hmm?
- Right.

492
00:24:30,042 --> 00:24:31,876
[Ms. Parker] Um, let's take it from…

493
00:24:31,959 --> 00:24:34,709
["Eventually" by Tame Impala
playing on speakers]

494
00:24:34,792 --> 00:24:36,292
[Carolyn] Another thing about Erin…

495
00:24:39,417 --> 00:24:40,501
You okay?

496
00:24:41,126 --> 00:24:41,959
Yeah.

497
00:24:42,042 --> 00:24:44,542
Are you sure? Do you wanna, like…

498
00:24:44,626 --> 00:24:46,376
No, no, no. Sorry. What were you saying?

499
00:24:46,459 --> 00:24:47,876
Um…

500
00:24:47,959 --> 00:24:51,709
Erin. She invited me
to this protest the other day,

501
00:24:51,792 --> 00:24:56,001
and instead, I just sat in the auditorium
and did nothing for three hours.

502
00:24:56,084 --> 00:24:58,001
You mean when we blocked the opening?

503
00:24:58,501 --> 00:25:01,542
- I'm literally gonna be in the shadows.
- You look so cool.

504
00:25:01,626 --> 00:25:04,917
- I mean, I'm excited for you.
- I'm excited for both of us.

505
00:25:05,834 --> 00:25:07,876
I have one line, Sophie.

506
00:25:07,959 --> 00:25:12,251
And your solo in "Club Knocked Up."
Come on, it's sounding so good. Belt it.

507
00:25:14,376 --> 00:25:15,917
<i>♪ Knock knock ♪</i>

508
00:25:17,876 --> 00:25:19,084
Nailed it.

509
00:25:19,167 --> 00:25:21,084
- [Caleb] I'll get there first.
- [Ethan] I will.

510
00:25:21,167 --> 00:25:24,084
[Ted] Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
Please, no running. Stop, don't move.

511
00:25:24,167 --> 00:25:26,584
Bring these to your friend Jeremy
and his dad.

512
00:25:26,667 --> 00:25:27,834
- Some of that.
- [Elizabeth] Hey.

513
00:25:27,917 --> 00:25:30,084
You really have to figure out
those driving lessons.

514
00:25:30,167 --> 00:25:32,251
Otherwise, you're gonna go off to college,

515
00:25:32,334 --> 00:25:35,167
and then you're gonna move
to New York and become a star,

516
00:25:35,251 --> 00:25:38,251
and then you'll be one of those
New Yorkers who never learned to drive.

517
00:25:38,334 --> 00:25:40,001
- I'll hire a hot chauffeur.
- [laughs]

518
00:25:40,084 --> 00:25:41,792
- [Ethan] No, Jeremy, stop!
- [woman] Just…

519
00:25:41,876 --> 00:25:43,292
- [Ethan] Jeremy, stop!
- What was that?

520
00:25:43,376 --> 00:25:45,626
- [Caleb] Gimme the pickle.
- [Ethan] I want that bagel!

521
00:25:45,709 --> 00:25:49,459
Okay, but what about when you fall in love
with your hot chauffeur

522
00:25:49,542 --> 00:25:53,167
and get married and have kids
and then you have to drive them to school?

523
00:25:53,792 --> 00:25:55,042
Why can't he drive them?

524
00:25:55,126 --> 00:25:58,417
Because you will be better at it
because I taught you how to drive.

525
00:25:58,501 --> 00:25:59,459
Mmm.

526
00:25:59,542 --> 00:26:01,292
Women's rights.

527
00:26:01,376 --> 00:26:02,876
Fine, teach me to drive.

528
00:26:02,959 --> 00:26:05,376
Okay. Tomorrow, after school?

529
00:26:05,459 --> 00:26:06,459
[Sophie] Uh, let me see.

530
00:26:07,501 --> 00:26:10,542
- Ugh. Shoot. Rehearsal.
- [Ted] You wanna wear the shoes?

531
00:26:10,626 --> 00:26:12,959
- You can't act like that. Come on.
- [Caleb] I'm telling Mom.

532
00:26:13,584 --> 00:26:15,376
[Elizabeth] Ugh, what happened?

533
00:26:15,459 --> 00:26:18,376
Ethan called Jeremy Silcox a dipshit.

534
00:26:18,917 --> 00:26:20,167
[Elizabeth laughs]

535
00:26:22,001 --> 00:26:23,751
- Wanna just go now?
- [Sophie] Yeah.

536
00:26:24,626 --> 00:26:26,709
- Some of the songs are really hard.
- Mmm.

537
00:26:26,792 --> 00:26:30,251
I've been listening to the recordings,
and she just… she sounds so good.

538
00:26:30,334 --> 00:26:32,292
- And I just--
- Yeah, 'cause it's a recording.

539
00:26:32,376 --> 00:26:34,126
You know, she had so many chances,

540
00:26:34,209 --> 00:26:37,667
and she had so much time to figure it out.

541
00:26:37,751 --> 00:26:39,626
You have time too, sweetie.

542
00:26:40,292 --> 00:26:41,542
[Sophie sighs]

543
00:26:42,626 --> 00:26:43,542
What?

544
00:26:43,626 --> 00:26:44,876
- [retches]
- Mom!

545
00:26:46,167 --> 00:26:47,459
- [Sophie] Oh…
- [Elizabeth gasps]

546
00:26:47,542 --> 00:26:49,709
Oh, don't look, honey. Please don't look.

547
00:26:49,792 --> 00:26:51,792
[coughing and gasping]

548
00:26:53,459 --> 00:26:55,001
Oh! [gasps]

549
00:26:55,084 --> 00:26:57,084
[breathing heavily]

550
00:26:58,001 --> 00:27:00,001
[gentle, poignant music playing]

551
00:27:08,001 --> 00:27:11,334
- [poignant music builds]
- [no in-scene audio]

552
00:27:18,167 --> 00:27:20,167
[music continues]

553
00:27:36,834 --> 00:27:38,834
[gentle music continues]

554
00:27:46,001 --> 00:27:47,417
[Elizabeth] <i>I know he said it's worse</i>

555
00:27:47,501 --> 00:27:50,459
<i>and spreading faster</i>
<i>than he thought it would, but…</i>

556
00:27:51,167 --> 00:27:53,167
Can't be happening that fast, right?

557
00:27:53,251 --> 00:27:54,792
Lizzie, I don't know.

558
00:27:54,876 --> 00:27:58,334
Maybe the end of July or August?

559
00:27:58,417 --> 00:28:00,959
He said he couldn't say.
I really… I don't think he knows.

560
00:28:01,042 --> 00:28:03,501
I know he said, you know,
travel isn't a good idea,

561
00:28:03,584 --> 00:28:06,042
but we can't not go to the beach house.

562
00:28:06,126 --> 00:28:08,292
- Yeah.
- I already told Sophie.

563
00:28:08,917 --> 00:28:12,001
Oh, God. And the show.
The show is so important to her.

564
00:28:12,584 --> 00:28:13,709
[sighs]

565
00:28:16,792 --> 00:28:18,417
Let's not tell them.

566
00:28:19,251 --> 00:28:20,751
Just not yet.

567
00:28:21,251 --> 00:28:22,667
Well, what about Soph?

568
00:28:22,751 --> 00:28:25,292
- She'll quit the show.
- She's gonna want to know.

569
00:28:25,376 --> 00:28:28,667
She has something that makes her happy,
and I can't let her lose that too.

570
00:28:28,751 --> 00:28:30,459
They're gonna see what's happening.

571
00:28:33,751 --> 00:28:38,126
Okay, we can tell them…
tell them that I'm struggling, but not…

572
00:28:41,251 --> 00:28:42,959
And then, after the show,

573
00:28:43,834 --> 00:28:45,334
we go to the Crane House.

574
00:28:45,417 --> 00:28:47,042
- We'll all be together.
- Okay.

575
00:28:47,626 --> 00:28:49,959
- And we can just tell them there.
- Great.

576
00:28:50,917 --> 00:28:54,542
I think, in the meantime,
we can ask my parents to come help.

577
00:28:54,626 --> 00:28:57,876
- Yeah. Whatever you want.
- Well, it's definitely not what I want.

578
00:28:57,959 --> 00:29:01,209
- Uh… I know.
- But I just… think we're gonna need them.

579
00:29:01,834 --> 00:29:03,001
But oh, my mom.

580
00:29:03,084 --> 00:29:04,334
[sighs]

581
00:29:04,417 --> 00:29:07,417
I'll take care of it.
Okay? I don't want you to worry.

582
00:29:07,501 --> 00:29:10,376
I mean, I kind of need
something to worry about that's not…

583
00:29:11,042 --> 00:29:12,584
that's not it.

584
00:29:15,876 --> 00:29:19,834
Is… "it" your mom?

585
00:29:20,626 --> 00:29:21,501
Or…

586
00:29:21,584 --> 00:29:23,834
It's my mom? Uh, it's the…

587
00:29:23,917 --> 00:29:26,834
- You… you said "it."
- It's the cancer.

588
00:29:28,292 --> 00:29:30,209
- I got… I got con…
- [laughs]

589
00:29:30,876 --> 00:29:32,334
I got confused.

590
00:29:33,209 --> 00:29:35,209
[phone ringing]

591
00:29:36,834 --> 00:29:39,792
- Hello?
- [Ted] <i>Maybe I'm hopped up on coffee and…</i>

592
00:29:39,876 --> 00:29:41,834
[Elizabeth laughs]

593
00:29:41,917 --> 00:29:42,751
Dad?

594
00:29:43,251 --> 00:29:47,542
[Elizabeth] <i>You thought I would say "it"?</i>
<i>You thought I would call her "it"?</i>

595
00:29:47,626 --> 00:29:50,001
- [laughing]
- [Ted] <i>I won't tell anybody.</i>

596
00:29:50,542 --> 00:29:51,792
<i>Especially it.</i>

597
00:29:51,876 --> 00:29:53,876
[Elizabeth and Ted laughing]

598
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:56,167
- [laughs]
- [Elizabeth] <i>Yeah.</i>

599
00:29:57,126 --> 00:29:58,584
<i>Oh my God.</i>

600
00:29:59,209 --> 00:30:01,626
- [laughing] <i>Oh my God!</i>
- [Ted] <i>That's so cute.</i>

601
00:30:03,167 --> 00:30:04,417
[Elizabeth sighs]

602
00:30:05,292 --> 00:30:08,417
- I'm sure I got the wrong cheese.
- I think the cheese is fine.

603
00:30:08,501 --> 00:30:10,084
[Ethan] Mom, Mom, they're here!

604
00:30:14,042 --> 00:30:16,584
- Doorbell doesn't work.
- It's this one, Grandpa Dale.

605
00:30:16,667 --> 00:30:17,501
- [bell rings]
- Oh!

606
00:30:17,584 --> 00:30:19,459
Joke never gets old, huh, Dale?

607
00:30:19,542 --> 00:30:20,792
- Boys, quit it. Enough.
- Okay.

608
00:30:20,876 --> 00:30:23,251
- When did you get so big?
- [Ted] Hug your grandmother, please.

609
00:30:23,334 --> 00:30:24,667
Come over here, you!

610
00:30:24,751 --> 00:30:26,584
Oh! Oh my goodness.

611
00:30:26,667 --> 00:30:28,459
[Ted] All right, boys, inside. Let's go.

612
00:30:29,959 --> 00:30:30,959
Oh!

613
00:30:31,667 --> 00:30:34,917
- Excuse me, who is this woman?
- [laughs]

614
00:30:35,001 --> 00:30:37,709
- Sophie, you're so gorgeous.
- Thank you.

615
00:30:37,792 --> 00:30:40,917
- Oh, God. Where's your mother?
- She's right there.

616
00:30:41,501 --> 00:30:44,251
- [grandmother] Oh, my baby.
- Hi, Mom.

617
00:30:46,626 --> 00:30:49,459
[Caleb] Why are Grandpa Dale and Lala
staying in my room?

618
00:30:49,542 --> 00:30:51,459
[Ted] Because you only
sleep in Ethan's room.

619
00:30:51,542 --> 00:30:53,751
Yeah, but why do I have
to sleep on the trundle?

620
00:30:53,834 --> 00:30:56,292
You literally refuse
to sleep anyplace else.

621
00:30:56,376 --> 00:30:57,917
How long are they staying?

622
00:30:58,626 --> 00:31:00,584
- [grandmother] Uh…
- Um, we don't know.

623
00:31:00,667 --> 00:31:04,084
Yeah, and your mom said I might be able
to give you driving lessons?

624
00:31:04,167 --> 00:31:06,501
Yeah, that'd be fun. Totally.

625
00:31:08,459 --> 00:31:11,251
- Well, you guys must be starving.
- Come on, boys, let's go upstairs.

626
00:31:11,334 --> 00:31:13,876
- Bring the bags.
- [Ethan] I wanna carry Grandpa's suitcase.

627
00:31:13,959 --> 00:31:15,542
- [Caleb] No, I do! I do!
- [grandmother] Oh.

628
00:31:15,626 --> 00:31:17,084
[Ted] Forget where the stairs are?

629
00:31:17,167 --> 00:31:20,167
Oh. Oh. Well, uh…

630
00:31:20,959 --> 00:31:24,126
I'm off creamy cheeses.
It's not good for my gut.

631
00:31:24,209 --> 00:31:25,167
Oh.

632
00:31:27,584 --> 00:31:28,459
[Dale] But, um…

633
00:31:29,042 --> 00:31:29,959
I'll have a grape.

634
00:31:30,042 --> 00:31:31,959
- Just a grape?
- [Dale] Yeah. Whoa.

635
00:31:33,917 --> 00:31:34,834
Thank you.

636
00:31:36,459 --> 00:31:37,626
Just one grape?

637
00:31:37,709 --> 00:31:40,251
So after you come back
in the door, Sophie,

638
00:31:40,334 --> 00:31:42,876
um, you grab him,
and that's where the kiss happens.

639
00:31:43,667 --> 00:31:44,917
[whispers] Where's Carolyn?

640
00:31:46,126 --> 00:31:48,376
Do you feel okay about that, Sophie?

641
00:31:49,042 --> 00:31:51,126
Oh, uh… I don't know.

642
00:31:51,876 --> 00:31:55,334
[Ms. Parker] Well, we can do something
other than a kiss. Like a hug or…

643
00:31:55,834 --> 00:31:57,501
- Jack, what do you think?
- Oh, uh…

644
00:31:57,584 --> 00:32:00,251
- I did a kiss last year. I'm cool.
- Yeah. I'm cool too, then.

645
00:32:00,334 --> 00:32:02,667
Okay, great. So why don't we try one?

646
00:32:03,292 --> 00:32:04,251
Okay.

647
00:32:13,626 --> 00:32:15,001
[door slams loudly]

648
00:32:18,292 --> 00:32:20,251
Sophie, you have to kiss him.

649
00:32:20,751 --> 00:32:21,834
Yes.

650
00:32:41,501 --> 00:32:42,417
[Ms. Parker] Good.

651
00:32:43,542 --> 00:32:47,167
The thing is, right now, Jenna is thinking
she's made a huge mistake,

652
00:32:47,251 --> 00:32:48,834
so maybe, mmm…

653
00:32:49,542 --> 00:32:50,376
less smiley.

654
00:32:50,459 --> 00:32:51,292
Oh.

655
00:32:51,792 --> 00:32:55,126
Yeah. Um, sorry,
I was just trying an acting choice.

656
00:32:55,209 --> 00:32:56,792
Yeah? Great.

657
00:32:57,584 --> 00:32:59,459
- Do you wanna try it again?
- Yes.

658
00:33:02,084 --> 00:33:04,084
["She Used to Be Mine" playing
through earbuds]

659
00:33:04,167 --> 00:33:07,626
[grandmother] …Dale and I to come here
and say, "Let's straighten this out."

660
00:33:07,709 --> 00:33:09,334
No, listen to me.

661
00:33:09,417 --> 00:33:12,292
Our neighbor can get her into Dana-Farber.

662
00:33:12,376 --> 00:33:14,792
Their cancer team
is top three in the country.

663
00:33:14,876 --> 00:33:17,667
- [Ted] That's what all the hospitals say.
- [grandmother] They really are.

664
00:33:17,751 --> 00:33:19,792
[Ted] Listen. We're doing
everything that we can.

665
00:33:19,876 --> 00:33:21,751
We trust Dr. Steckman and his team.

666
00:33:21,834 --> 00:33:24,209
- Who is Dr. Steckman? What hospital is--
- [Ted] You know him!

667
00:33:24,292 --> 00:33:27,126
- [grandmother] I've never met the man.
- [Ted] The same doctor from last time!

668
00:33:27,209 --> 00:33:29,667
- [buzz of conversation]
- [girl] Right. So, um…

669
00:33:30,792 --> 00:33:33,209
I can't believe I missed you guys kissing.

670
00:33:33,292 --> 00:33:35,834
I'm telling you,
the chemistry was undeniable.

671
00:33:35,917 --> 00:33:38,042
Okay, remember when we made out
with those guys at camp,

672
00:33:38,126 --> 00:33:41,667
and we were like, "Ew, it's so slimy,"
and we didn't get what the big deal was?

673
00:33:41,751 --> 00:33:45,042
I get what the big deal is now. Like,
We were just kissing the wrong people.

674
00:33:45,126 --> 00:33:47,334
Hey, Carolyn, you forgot this.

675
00:33:47,417 --> 00:33:48,751
[Carolyn] Oh, thanks.

676
00:33:48,834 --> 00:33:50,917
My legs are killing me from yesterday.

677
00:33:51,001 --> 00:33:52,542
- You?
- Yesterday?

678
00:33:53,167 --> 00:33:57,001
Yeah, we did this hike after school.
I thought it was gonna be like two miles,

679
00:33:57,084 --> 00:33:59,917
and then it ended up
being four and a half miles.

680
00:34:00,001 --> 00:34:00,876
Cool.

681
00:34:01,876 --> 00:34:02,751
Yeah.

682
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:06,459
You should totally come with us next time.

683
00:34:06,542 --> 00:34:08,042
Thank you, that's sweet.

684
00:34:09,959 --> 00:34:11,626
You told me
you had a doctor's appointment.

685
00:34:11,709 --> 00:34:14,126
I had to get a ride home
with Trista and her mom.

686
00:34:15,126 --> 00:34:16,459
Wait, are you quitting the show?

687
00:34:18,834 --> 00:34:20,459
I already did.

688
00:34:21,042 --> 00:34:22,459
And you didn't tell me?

689
00:34:23,376 --> 00:34:25,584
- I don't know. I didn't know how.
- I am so sorry.

690
00:34:25,667 --> 00:34:27,834
- I didn't know. Yeah.
- It's okay. Can you just give us…

691
00:34:30,001 --> 00:34:31,959
You have a lot going on, so I--

692
00:34:32,042 --> 00:34:35,042
Yeah, you're right, I do have
a lot going on right now. I need to focus.

693
00:34:35,126 --> 00:34:37,334
- Soph, I wanted to--
- Don't worry about driving me anymore.

694
00:34:37,417 --> 00:34:40,834
My grandpa's just sitting around all day
with nothing to do. He loves to drive.

695
00:34:40,917 --> 00:34:41,834
Sophie!

696
00:34:43,792 --> 00:34:46,376
I need more practice.
Can we do extra rehearsals?

697
00:34:46,459 --> 00:34:47,459
Mmm…

698
00:34:47,542 --> 00:34:50,834
I'd rather devote my spare time
to lesson plans about Mesopotamia

699
00:34:50,917 --> 00:34:53,876
and the spice trade routes
along the Tigris and Euphrates rivers.

700
00:34:53,959 --> 00:34:54,917
Okay.

701
00:34:56,334 --> 00:34:58,584
I'm kidding! That's so boring!

702
