1378
01:10:39,792 --> 01:10:41,209
I wish you didn't do that.

1379
01:10:41,292 --> 01:10:43,792
- I just wanted to see you. I'm sorry.
- Mom, you should've asked me!

1380
01:10:43,876 --> 01:10:45,751
I… I didn't want to get your hopes up.

1381
01:10:45,834 --> 01:10:48,792
- In case I was feeling too sick.
- You can talk to me! I'm not a little kid!

1382
01:10:48,876 --> 01:10:51,209
I know. I know that.
You're growing up so fast.

1383
01:10:51,292 --> 01:10:56,334
- I feel like I'm… missing so much--
- Mom, you told me to do the show!

1384
01:10:56,417 --> 01:10:59,876
I did, yes, and of course
you should have done the show.

1385
01:10:59,959 --> 01:11:01,626
But I didn't know you were…

1386
01:11:01,709 --> 01:11:02,751
[sobs]

1387
01:11:03,917 --> 01:11:06,584
- You didn't tell me.
- I wanted to fight it.

1388
01:11:06,667 --> 01:11:10,376
I wanted to fight it,
and I tried so hard. I've been trying.

1389
01:11:10,459 --> 01:11:13,126
If you had told me, I wouldn't have
worked so much on the show.

1390
01:11:13,209 --> 01:11:17,792
You were so excited about it, honey.
I didn't want to ruin it for you.

1391
01:11:17,876 --> 01:11:19,501
You should have let <i>me </i>choose!

1392
01:11:19,584 --> 01:11:22,084
- You're right.
- I asked for extra rehearsals.

1393
01:11:22,167 --> 01:11:23,876
- Oh, honey.
- I'm not good enough.

1394
01:11:23,959 --> 01:11:26,126
- And I didn't wanna be around here.
- You're great.

1395
01:11:26,209 --> 01:11:29,042
- And me and Carolyn have been so weird.
- What happened with Carolyn?

1396
01:11:29,126 --> 01:11:31,834
- And now everything's awful.
- Honey.

1397
01:11:33,042 --> 01:11:36,084
Honey, I know things are hard. I know.

1398
01:11:36,167 --> 01:11:39,834
But… but, please…
You… you're so wonderful.

1399
01:11:39,917 --> 01:11:42,917
- Mom, do not lie about that too.
- I'm not lying!

1400
01:11:43,001 --> 01:11:45,626
- I'm not lying.
- Yes, you are! It's terrible! I'm terrible!

1401
01:11:45,709 --> 01:11:48,751
- No. No, no, no. Honey, no.
- [sobbing]

1402
01:11:48,834 --> 01:11:51,584
Listen to me.
Sophie, just look at me, okay?

1403
01:11:53,084 --> 01:11:55,917
I'm so sorry I didn't tell you.

1404
01:11:58,209 --> 01:11:59,876
I don't know how to do this.

1405
01:12:00,459 --> 01:12:02,167
- Mom, just…
- It's hard.

1406
01:12:02,251 --> 01:12:03,292
Just say it.

1407
01:12:03,376 --> 01:12:04,459
[sighs]

1408
01:12:06,251 --> 01:12:08,084
- Sophie.
- Say it.

1409
01:12:09,834 --> 01:12:10,834
[sighs]

1410
01:12:13,709 --> 01:12:15,542
I'm not gonna make it.

1411
01:12:17,251 --> 01:12:19,167
[sobbing] No, no, no.

1412
01:12:21,417 --> 01:12:22,667
No.

1413
01:12:23,251 --> 01:12:24,292
[Elizabeth] Hey.

1414
01:12:29,959 --> 01:12:31,001
[sniffles]

1415
01:12:31,084 --> 01:12:33,084
[sobbing]

1416
01:12:37,001 --> 01:12:39,459
- [sighs]
- [footsteps going upstairs]

1417
01:12:43,292 --> 01:12:44,459
[sighs]

1418
01:12:44,542 --> 01:12:46,417
[emotional, somber music playing]

1419
01:13:01,042 --> 01:13:02,501
[birdsong]

1420
01:13:22,709 --> 01:13:25,167
[whispers] Can you wake up, please? Buddy.

1421
01:13:26,084 --> 01:13:27,084
Wake up.

1422
01:13:27,667 --> 01:13:31,001
Hi, how'd you sleep? Good morning.

1423
01:13:53,292 --> 01:13:55,709
- [Sophie] Bye. Love you.
- [Caleb] Bye, Sophie. Bye, Dad.

1424
01:13:55,792 --> 01:13:58,501
You good? You've got everything? Goodbye.

1425
01:13:59,167 --> 01:14:01,167
[school bell rings][sighs heavily]

1426
01:14:12,584 --> 01:14:13,709
You okay?

1427
01:14:15,584 --> 01:14:16,667
No.

1428
01:14:17,834 --> 01:14:18,917
Are you?

1429
01:14:20,376 --> 01:14:22,376
[sighs heavily]

1430
01:14:25,417 --> 01:14:26,292
No.

1431
01:14:27,751 --> 01:14:30,542
Soph, everything that's happening
is so unfair.

1432
01:14:32,626 --> 01:14:36,001
It's unfair for you, for me,
for your brothers, for Mom.

1433
01:14:36,084 --> 01:14:38,376
- [sniffles]
- Yeah.

1434
01:14:38,459 --> 01:14:41,792
I know all she's trying to do
is make it hurt less, but I don't…

1435
01:14:45,459 --> 01:14:47,042
I don't think that's possible.

1436
01:14:49,209 --> 01:14:50,417
[sniffles]

1437
01:14:50,501 --> 01:14:54,626
And I so wish we could just fast-forward
to the part where you forgive us, but…

1438
01:14:55,376 --> 01:14:57,459
I know that's not possible either.

1439
01:14:58,667 --> 01:15:00,167
I hate you're going through this,

1440
01:15:00,251 --> 01:15:03,251
because every time I look at you,
all I see is how much I love you.

1441
01:15:07,959 --> 01:15:09,584
It's what Mom sees too.

1442
01:15:22,167 --> 01:15:23,584
[music fades]

1443
01:15:23,667 --> 01:15:25,709
[Carolyn] I'm with you for all of it.

1444
01:15:26,584 --> 01:15:28,834
No matter what, okay?

1445
01:15:32,459 --> 01:15:35,417
Also, I got you something.

1446
01:15:39,334 --> 01:15:40,626
[laughs]

1447
01:15:40,709 --> 01:15:45,209
I know I'm not in the play, but it doesn't
mean that all the traditions have to end.

1448
01:15:45,709 --> 01:15:47,376
It's really cute. Thank you.

1449
01:15:48,042 --> 01:15:50,292
- To a good show.
- Mmm!

1450
01:15:50,376 --> 01:15:52,834
- Mmm!
- Mmm! [laughs]

1451
01:15:54,001 --> 01:15:55,501
Uh, and Sophie,

1452
01:15:56,001 --> 01:15:58,417
me and Erin are so excited to see you.

1453
01:15:59,334 --> 01:16:01,876
And we're, uh…

1454
01:16:01,959 --> 01:16:05,667
I know. The chemistry is undeniable.

1455
01:16:05,751 --> 01:16:06,917
[chuckles]

1456
01:16:07,667 --> 01:16:09,751
At least one of us
is kissing the right person.

1457
01:16:11,542 --> 01:16:12,792
- Come here.
- [laughs]

1458
01:16:12,876 --> 01:16:14,542
[upbeat, warm music playing]

1459
01:16:14,626 --> 01:16:16,751
- [Carolyn] So cute!
- [Sophie] I know, right?

1460
01:16:27,417 --> 01:16:29,042
[Ms. Parker] Thanks, guys.

1461
01:16:29,126 --> 01:16:32,001
- [Mr. Stewart] You ready for tonight?
- [Ms. Parker] Hey, guys.

1462
01:16:32,084 --> 01:16:34,501
- [Mr. Stewart] Come in. It's time.
- [boy 1] Yeah!

1463
01:16:35,792 --> 01:16:37,876
- [girl 1] Yeah, I'm sure you did.
- [girl 2] How many?

1464
01:16:49,834 --> 01:16:52,001
- [phone alert chimes]
- [boy] All right, let's do it.

1465
01:17:00,667 --> 01:17:02,126
You can play Jenna, right?

1466
01:17:02,917 --> 01:17:04,292
And Audrey knows Dawn?

1467
01:17:05,001 --> 01:17:06,126
Excuse me?

1468
01:17:06,792 --> 01:17:09,334
I'm sorry, I have to go.
You'll be better than me anyway.

1469
01:17:12,792 --> 01:17:13,626
I'll be amazing.

1470
01:17:15,001 --> 01:17:16,209
[tires screech]

1471
01:17:16,292 --> 01:17:18,084
- Thank you, TJ.
- Love you, Soph.

1472
01:17:19,501 --> 01:17:20,876
- [door slams]
- [Sophie] Mom?

1473
01:17:28,667 --> 01:17:29,959
[sniffles]

1474
01:17:33,709 --> 01:17:35,167
I'm really scared.

1475
01:17:37,167 --> 01:17:38,292
Me too.

1476
01:17:39,334 --> 01:17:41,334
I'm so sorry, sweetheart.

1477
01:17:41,417 --> 01:17:42,584
Me too.

1478
01:17:45,917 --> 01:17:50,542
But if we're both scared,
who's gonna take care of us?

1479
01:17:52,001 --> 01:17:54,209
Your hot chauffeur husband.

1480
01:17:54,292 --> 01:17:56,126
[laughs]

1481
01:17:56,209 --> 01:17:58,876
Well, what if there is
no hot chauffeur husband?

1482
01:17:59,459 --> 01:18:02,084
Then I guess we'll have
to take care of ourselves.

1483
01:18:02,751 --> 01:18:04,292
- Women's rights.
- [laughs]

1484
01:18:06,501 --> 01:18:09,459
Wait. Shouldn't you be getting
into costume right now?

1485
01:18:10,042 --> 01:18:12,459
I don't want to miss
another minute with you.

1486
01:18:12,542 --> 01:18:13,751
[Elizabeth] Oh…

1487
01:18:14,417 --> 01:18:16,376
Oh, honey, no.

1488
01:18:16,917 --> 01:18:17,917
[sighs]

1489
01:18:19,792 --> 01:18:20,792
[sighs]

1490
01:18:20,876 --> 01:18:22,667
Your second-grade concert…

1491
01:18:22,751 --> 01:18:25,251
You cried so much. You were so proud.

1492
01:18:25,334 --> 01:18:26,501
I know.

1493
01:18:26,584 --> 01:18:28,209
No, wait. Wait. [sniffles]

1494
01:18:31,084 --> 01:18:36,626
I had looked for years
for a thing that lit me up.

1495
01:18:38,459 --> 01:18:41,292
And you found it by seven.

1496
01:18:42,459 --> 01:18:44,376
I cried because I thought,

1497
01:18:45,709 --> 01:18:47,292
no matter what,

1498
01:18:48,626 --> 01:18:53,209
you could return to that light
and you'd be okay.

1499
01:18:53,876 --> 01:18:56,334
But I don't wanna do the show without you.

1500
01:18:56,417 --> 01:18:58,417
I don't wanna do any of it without you.

1501
01:18:58,501 --> 01:19:00,834
You're never gonna be without me.

1502
01:19:04,959 --> 01:19:06,167
[sniffles]

1503
01:19:07,084 --> 01:19:10,209
I'm sorry you never found
the thing that lit you up.

1504
01:19:11,084 --> 01:19:12,792
But I did. [sniffles]

1505
01:19:18,001 --> 01:19:20,001
[band tuning up]

1506
01:19:25,209 --> 01:19:28,376
[Ted] Right here, this is us. This is us.
All the way in. All the way in. Okay,

1507
01:19:28,459 --> 01:19:31,209
- Whee! Whoo!
- [Ted sighs heavily]

1508
01:19:31,292 --> 01:19:33,292
- Whoo!
- [seat squeaking]

1509
01:19:42,209 --> 01:19:43,876
[outgoing call ringing]

1510
01:19:44,584 --> 01:19:46,167
[ringing]

1511
01:19:48,167 --> 01:19:49,042
Elizabeth?

1512
01:19:50,042 --> 01:19:51,834
You should be in Sophie's life.

1513
01:19:51,917 --> 01:19:57,084
You should be in all of their lives.
I… just need you to listen to her.

1514
01:19:57,167 --> 01:19:58,334
[gasps]

1515
01:19:59,251 --> 01:20:02,001
Uh… I will. I promise I will.

1516
01:20:02,584 --> 01:20:03,834
<i>- Okay?</i>
- [sighs]

1517
01:20:03,917 --> 01:20:06,334
<i>I love you so much, Elizabeth.</i>

1518
01:20:07,334 --> 01:20:09,042
[sobs] I love you too, Mom.

1519
01:20:10,167 --> 01:20:12,834
<i>You can tell her stories about me?</i>

1520
01:20:12,917 --> 01:20:14,667
You have all the stories.

1521
01:20:16,084 --> 01:20:18,251
<i>- I know that this is last-minute.</i>
- [mouths]

1522
01:20:18,334 --> 01:20:19,834
<i>I'm sorry, but…</i>

1523
01:20:20,542 --> 01:20:22,584
I know it would mean a lot to her
if you could

1524
01:20:22,667 --> 01:20:25,751
make it to closing night
of her show tomorrow.

1525
01:20:26,334 --> 01:20:27,459
[Linda] <i>Um…</i>

1526
01:20:27,542 --> 01:20:30,542
Is tonight okay instead?

1527
01:20:33,251 --> 01:20:34,459
[chuckles]

1528
01:20:35,042 --> 01:20:36,542
Of course, you're there already.

1529
01:20:36,626 --> 01:20:40,251
No, well, I'm sorry. Your father
said we shouldn't, but I insisted.

1530
01:20:40,334 --> 01:20:41,459
[Elizabeth chuckles]

1531
01:20:41,542 --> 01:20:42,834
- [car horn blares]
- [tires squeal]

1532
01:20:42,917 --> 01:20:46,292
- [man] Hey, hey!
- [Sophie] Oh, I'm sorry! No, no! Oh, no!

1533
01:20:47,084 --> 01:20:48,084
Oh my God.

1534
01:20:52,126 --> 01:20:53,376
[car lock bleeps]

1535
01:20:53,959 --> 01:20:55,667
- I'm so sorry, but--
- [Mallory] Don't worry.

1536
01:20:57,001 --> 01:20:58,042
I stalled.

1537
01:20:58,542 --> 01:20:59,959
I knew you'd come back.

1538
01:21:00,542 --> 01:21:04,042
And, um…
I like playing Dawn better anyway.

1539
01:21:04,126 --> 01:21:05,459
[chuckles]

1540
01:21:05,542 --> 01:21:07,792
- Are you wearing driving gloves?
- What? No.

1541
01:21:07,876 --> 01:21:09,876
[applause]

1542
01:21:16,709 --> 01:21:18,709
[girl] You're gonna do great, Sophie.

1543
01:21:20,751 --> 01:21:22,334
Hey, Sophie.

1544
01:21:22,417 --> 01:21:24,709
- I like your dress.
- Thank you.

1545
01:21:28,042 --> 01:21:30,042
[piano playing "She Used to Be Mine"]

1546
01:21:34,709 --> 01:21:37,959
<i>♪ It's not simple to say ♪</i>

1547
01:21:38,917 --> 01:21:44,792
<i>♪ That most days I don't recognize me ♪</i>

1548
01:21:44,876 --> 01:21:50,792
<i>♪ That these shoes and this apron</i>
<i>That place and its patrons ♪</i>

1549
01:21:50,876 --> 01:21:55,626
<i>♪ Have taken more than I gave them ♪</i>

1550
01:21:57,626 --> 01:22:01,126
<i>♪ It's not easy to know ♪</i>

1551
01:22:01,709 --> 01:22:06,876
<i>♪ I'm not anything like I used to be ♪</i>

1552
01:22:06,959 --> 01:22:10,834
<i>♪ Although it's true I was never ♪</i>

1553
01:22:10,917 --> 01:22:13,959
<i>♪ Attention's sweet center ♪</i>

1554
01:22:14,042 --> 01:22:18,001
<i>♪ I still remember that girl ♪</i>

1555
01:22:19,126 --> 01:22:23,917
<i>♪ She's imperfect, but she tries ♪</i>

1556
01:22:24,626 --> 01:22:29,626
<i>♪ She is good, but she lies ♪</i>

1557
01:22:30,501 --> 01:22:35,126
<i>♪ She is hard on herself ♪</i>

1558
01:22:36,167 --> 01:22:40,626
<i>♪ She is broken and won't ask for help ♪</i>

1559
01:22:42,209 --> 01:22:47,001
<i>♪ She is messy, but she's kind ♪</i>

1560
01:22:47,917 --> 01:22:53,751
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

1561
01:22:53,834 --> 01:22:56,709
<i>♪ She is all of this mixed up ♪</i>

1562
01:22:56,792 --> 01:23:01,167
<i>♪ And baked in a beautiful pie ♪</i>

1563
01:23:02,292 --> 01:23:05,876
<i>♪ She is gone, but she used to be ♪</i>

1564
01:23:05,959 --> 01:23:10,126
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1565
01:23:12,667 --> 01:23:16,292
<i>♪ It's not what I asked for ♪</i>

1566
01:23:16,376 --> 01:23:19,001
<i>♪ Sometimes life ♪</i>

1567
01:23:19,709 --> 01:23:22,959
<i>♪ Just slips in through a back door ♪</i>

1568
01:23:23,042 --> 01:23:25,876
<i>♪ And carves out a person ♪</i>

1569
01:23:25,959 --> 01:23:30,126
<i>♪ And makes you believe it's all true ♪</i>

1570
01:23:31,626 --> 01:23:34,126
<i>♪ And now I've got you ♪</i>

1571
01:23:35,501 --> 01:23:38,876
<i>♪ You're not what I asked for ♪</i>

1572
01:23:39,542 --> 01:23:45,167
<i>♪ If I'm honest</i>
<i>I know I would give it all back ♪</i>

1573
01:23:45,251 --> 01:23:48,334
<i>♪ For a chance to start over ♪</i>

1574
01:23:48,917 --> 01:23:53,459
<i>♪ And rewrite an ending or two ♪</i>

1575
01:23:54,042 --> 01:23:56,917
<i>♪ For that girl that I knew ♪</i>

1576
01:23:57,001 --> 01:24:01,501
<i>♪ Who was reckless just enough ♪</i>

1577
01:24:02,501 --> 01:24:04,376
<i>♪ Who gets hurt ♪</i>

1578
01:24:05,542 --> 01:24:08,417
<i>♪ But who learns how to toughen up ♪</i>

1579
01:24:08,501 --> 01:24:11,167
<i>♪ When she's bruised ♪</i>

1580
01:24:11,251 --> 01:24:17,001
<i>♪ And gets used by a man who can't love ♪</i>

1581
01:24:17,626 --> 01:24:23,292
<i>♪ And then she'll get stuck</i>
<i>And be scared ♪</i>

1582
01:24:23,376 --> 01:24:28,792
<i>♪ Of the life that's inside her</i>
<i>Growing stronger each day ♪</i>

1583
01:24:29,292 --> 01:24:34,542
<i>♪ Till it finally reminds her</i>
<i>To fight just a little ♪</i>

1584
01:24:35,126 --> 01:24:39,917
<i>♪ To bring back the fire in her eyes ♪</i>

1585
01:24:40,001 --> 01:24:44,167
<i>♪ That's been gone but used to be ♪</i>

1586
01:24:44,251 --> 01:24:50,751
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1587
01:24:53,001 --> 01:24:55,126
<i>♪ Oh, used to be ♪</i>

1588
01:24:55,876 --> 01:25:02,876
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1589
01:25:06,542 --> 01:25:08,167
<i>♪ She is messy ♪</i>

1590
01:25:09,042 --> 01:25:11,084
<i>♪ But she's kind ♪</i>

1591
01:25:12,084 --> 01:25:17,792
<i>♪ She is lonely most of the time ♪</i>

1592
01:25:17,876 --> 01:25:21,251
<i>♪ She is all of this mixed up ♪</i>

1593
01:25:21,334 --> 01:25:24,542
<i>♪ And baked in a beautiful pie ♪</i>

1594
01:25:29,251 --> 01:25:31,376
<i>♪ She is gone ♪</i>

1595
01:25:32,542 --> 01:25:35,667
<i>♪ But she used to be ♪</i>

1596
01:25:37,251 --> 01:25:43,667
<i>♪ Mine ♪</i>

1597
01:25:45,959 --> 01:25:48,167
[clapping]

1598
01:25:53,917 --> 01:25:55,917
[crickets chirping]

1599
01:25:59,209 --> 01:26:01,209
[crickets continue chirping]

1600
01:26:03,501 --> 01:26:05,709
["Silver Springs"
by Fleetwood Mac playing]

1601
01:26:24,334 --> 01:26:28,876
<i>♪ You could be my silver spring ♪</i>

1602
01:26:29,917 --> 01:26:34,001
<i>♪ Blue green, colors flashin' ♪</i>

1603
01:26:34,917 --> 01:26:39,001
<i>♪ I would be your only dream ♪</i>

1604
01:26:39,626 --> 01:26:42,209
<i>♪ Your shinin' autumn ♪</i>

1605
01:26:42,292 --> 01:26:46,917
<i>♪ Ocean crashin' ♪</i>

1606
01:26:48,376 --> 01:26:52,542
<i>♪ And don't say that she's pretty ♪</i>

1607
01:26:53,626 --> 01:26:57,917
<i>♪ And did you say that she loved you ♪</i>

1608
01:26:59,084 --> 01:27:03,167
<i>♪ Baby, I don't wanna know ♪</i>

1609
01:27:12,334 --> 01:27:16,584
<i>♪ So I'll begin not to love you ♪</i>

